Design a synchronous data latch that captures the value of a single-bit input (data_in) when the enable signal is high and the reset signal is low. When the reset signal (reset_l) is asserted low, the output (data_out) is set to zero. On the rising edge of the clock, if reset is not asserted, the latch either retains its current state or updates its output to the value of data_in based on the enable signal.
