description:
Design a combinational logic circuit that aggregates input values based on a 3-bit control signal. When `a` is 000, the output `b` is set to 1; when `a` is 001, it extracts 4 two-bit sections from the 4-bit input `c` and assigns them to the lower half of `b`. For control signals `a` equal to 010 and 011, the output `b` is set to fixed values of 3 and 4, respectively. For any other value of `a`, `b` defaults to 0. This module effectively acts as a specialized decoder that selects different output values based on the input conditions.
module top_module(
  input      [2:0] a,
  input      [3:0] c,

  output reg [7:0] b
);

code:
module top_module(
  input      [2:0] a,
  input      [3:0] c,

  output reg [7:0] b
);integer i;

  always @ (*)
  begin
    case(a)
      {3'b000}: b = 8'd1;
      {3'b001}:
        for(i=0;i<4;i=i+1) b[i*2+:2] = 2'(c[i]);
      {3'b010}: b = 8'd3;
      {3'b011}: b = 8'd4;
      default : b = 0;
    endcase
  end

endmodule

