description:
Develop a Continuous-Integrate-Comb (CIC) filter that processes a multi-bit input signal. The module features multiple input signals, configurable parameters for the number of stages and decimation factor, and integrates incoming samples before applying a comb filtering process. It utilizes an accumulator for the integrator section to sum input values across stages and maintains a delay line for the comb filtering, outputting a decimated sample based on the specified parameters. This design is essential for digital signal processing applications requiring low-pass filtering and downsampling.
module top_module(
  input clk, // Added clk input
  input [n*N-1:0] in,
  output reg [m-1:0] out // Changed out to reg type
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk, // Added clk input
  input [n*N-1:0] in,
  output reg [m-1:0] out // Changed out to reg type
);parameter n = 4; // number of input signals
parameter m = 2; // number of output signals
parameter R = 4; // decimation factor
parameter M = 3; // number of stages
parameter N = 8; // number of bits for each input signal

// Define accumulator for integrator section
reg [N-1:0] acc [0:M-1];
integer i;

// Define delay line for comb section
reg [N-1:0] delay [0:R-1];

// Implement integrator and comb sections
always @ (posedge clk) begin
  // Integrator section
  for (i = 0; i < M; i = i + 1) begin
    acc[i] <= acc[i] + in[i*N +: N];
  end

  // Comb section
